================================================================================
What is redistributed, and where
================================================================================

Two artifacts leave this repository, and they carry different obligations.

1. The source repository itself vendors no dependency. Cloning it and running
   `pnpm install` fetches packages from the npm registry under their own terms.

2. The container image ghcr.io/dasomel/narwhal-portal DOES redistribute them.
   `next build` produces a standalone server that bundles its runtime
   dependencies, and the Dockerfile copies that output into the image. Every
   attribution obligation therefore attaches to the image.

Next.js file tracing copies only the files the server needs, which strips
LICENSE files out of the output — a build of 1.0.17 had 631 LICENSE files under
node_modules and 3 under .next/standalone. THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md exists because
the build cannot be relied on to carry them.

