================================================================================
Deliberately NOT redistributed
================================================================================

sharp / libvips (@img/sharp-libvips-*, LGPL-3.0-or-later)

  Next.js pulls sharp into the standalone trace for its image optimizer. Its
  native backend libvips is LGPL-3.0-or-later, which would attach relinking and
  source-availability obligations to the image.

  The portal imports next/image nowhere, so the optimizer was never used. Image
  optimization is disabled and sharp is excluded from file tracing in
  next.config.ts; a standalone server built with those settings boots and serves
  routes with no module error. Verify a build with:

      find .next/standalone -ipath '*libvips*' -type f     # expect: no output

  If image optimization is ever enabled, sharp returns and this section must be
  replaced by a real LGPL notice.

